\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Can a deterministic algorithm polynomial in the total encoded length of any finite collection of ordinary strings return a common superstring of length at most twice the minimum?

\subsection{Short English statement}
Can a deterministic algorithm polynomial in the total encoded length of any finite collection of ordinary strings return a common superstring of length at most twice the minimum?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-Polynomial-Time-2-Approximation-for-Shortest-Common-Superstring-September-24-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

